From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 572/573] leds: rgb: add a driver for the AWINIC AW9120

The chip drives the Gemini PDA's indicator LEDs. Set each output's PWM
directly with a SETPWMI instruction written to CMDR, on channels handed to
I2C control through CTRS. The chip's SRAM engine, which runs fades and
loops by itself, isn't used; the LED core's software blink covers
indicators.

Reset the chip with the enable pin and check its ID before anything else.
Enable only the outputs in the device tree, at the limit each asks for, or
at 3.5 mA without one, which is the chip's lowest. The Gemian daemon's
per-channel current packing is off by one channel, so this follows the data
sheet instead.

Clear GCR.LEDE when nothing is lit, since that stops the chip's oscillator:
0.55 mA active against 130 uA standby. The rest of the configuration holds
without it.

Only compile-tested so far; no AW9120 has been driven by this code.
---
 drivers/leds/rgb/Kconfig       |  12 ++
 drivers/leds/rgb/Makefile      |   1 +
 drivers/leds/rgb/leds-aw9120.c | 363 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 376 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/leds/rgb/leds-aw9120.c

